---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const toml = `dhcp = true

[network_identity]
network_name = "my-smp"
network_secret = "use-a-random-secret"

[[peer]]
uri = "tcp://relay.example.com:11010"

# The Minecraft server's address on the network
[etmc]
server = "10.144.144.1:25565"
label = "My SMP"`;
---

<DocsLayout title="Config URLs" description="Let players join from a config file you host.">
  <p>
    Instead of sharing a link, a server admin can host a config file. It suits a server that's already on an
    EasyTier network, because the server doesn't need to run etmc.
  </p>

  <h2>For players</h2>
  <p>If the link starts with <code>etmc://v1/config/</code>, use it like any other link: paste it into
    <strong>Add Server</strong> or <strong>Direct Connect</strong>. etmc downloads the config each time you join.</p>
  <p>If you have a plain URL, choose <strong>Connect via config URL</strong> in the etmc menu and paste it, or run
    <code>/etmc connect &lt;url&gt;</code>.</p>

  <h2>For server admins</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Create the file with the <a href="/generator">generator</a>, or write it by hand.</li>
    <li>Host it at any HTTP or HTTPS URL.</li>
    <li>Put <code>etmc://v1/config/</code> in front of the URL and share that link, for example
      <code>etmc://v1/config/https://example.com/etmc.toml</code>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>When you change the file, players who saved the link get the change the next time they join, so you don't need
    to send a new link. Use HTTPS, so nobody can swap the file on its way to your players.</p>
  <p>The file is a normal EasyTier config, plus an <code>[etmc]</code> section that names the server:</p>
  <pre><code>{toml}</code></pre>
  <p>
    If you leave out <code>server</code>, players need the plain URL and enter the address themselves. An
    <code>etmc://v1/config/</code> link needs <code>server</code>, and only reads the network, secret, relays, server and
    label from the file. The URL can also serve an <code>etmc://</code> link instead of a config.
  </p>
  <div class="warn"><strong>Your secret isn't protected.</strong> It's plain text in this file, and anyone with the URL can read it and join. Keep it random, and never use a password you
    use anywhere else.</div>
</DocsLayout>
